Committed as `670cb23` ("Reduce accented Latin letters to their base in slugify").

One decision worth noting: I kept the letter/digit test as ASCII (`[a-z0-9]`), matching the original implementation's intent — non-Latin scripts still collapse to dashes. If you wanted to keep Unicode letters instead, that would be a separate change to the character class.

